\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The held-out probe on the final fits, per section. For each block and probe, the share of the block's within-type variance that the probe explains from $\mathbf  {z}$ beyond the permutation floor ($e^{2\,\mathrm  {excess}} - 1$, in \%): for the model trained without the adversary ($\alpha _a= 0$, two seeds), with it (the final fits, three seeds), and for the comparison methods on the same held-out cells. MintFlow and SIMVI have so far been run on the TMA core only (--: not yet run); on the serial section, MintFlow is the core's model transferred and SIMVI is fitted on the serial section itself. The \emph  {fraction left} is the excess with the adversary as a fraction of the mean excess without it: $0$ when the adversary removes everything the probe can find, $1$ when it removes nothing. Ranges are over seeds; Unassigned cells are not targets. The serial section of the TMA core is graded with the models fitted on the core.\relax }}{18}{table.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:probe}{{4}{18}{The held-out probe on the final fits, per section. For each block and probe, the share of the block's within-type variance that the probe explains from $\vz $ beyond the permutation floor ($e^{2\,\mathrm {excess}} - 1$, in \%): for the model trained without the adversary ($\alphaa = 0$, two seeds), with it (the final fits, three seeds), and for the comparison methods on the same held-out cells. MintFlow and SIMVI have so far been run on the TMA core only (--: not yet run); on the serial section, MintFlow is the core's model transferred and SIMVI is fitted on the serial section itself. The \emph {fraction left} is the excess with the adversary as a fraction of the mean excess without it: $0$ when the adversary removes everything the probe can find, $1$ when it removes nothing. Ranges are over seeds; Unassigned cells are not targets. The serial section of the TMA core is graded with the models fitted on the core.\relax }{table.caption.36}{}}
